.1,"_gate_sbc_dilution":0.033962159001331045,"_gp_sbc_dilution":false,"_score_sbc_dilution":43.4,"_gate_insider_own":0.00338,"_gp_insider_own":false,"_score_insider_own":2.3,"_gate_insider_buying":0.0,"_gp_insider_buying":false,"_score_insider_buying":0.0,"pf":[],"description_full":"FactSet Research Systems Inc., together with its subsidiaries, operates as a global data and artificial intelligence solutions provider for the financial markets in the Americas, Europe, the Middle East, Africa, and Asia Pacific. It offers data, products, and analytical applications; and workstations, portfolio analytics, and enterprise data solutions, as well as managed services for supporting data, performance, risk and reporting, and AI-enabled workflows. The company also provides financial data and market intelligence on securities, companies, industries, and people that enable clients to research advisory, dealmaking and investment ideas, as well as analyze, monitor, and manage portfolios; and solutions covering investment lifecycle of investment research, portfolio construction and analysis, trade execution, performance measurement, risk management, and reporting. In addition, it offers banking solutions that supports company and market research; wealth solutions which supports home office, advisory, and client engagement workflows; and data and technology offerings, including desktop and mobile platform, data solutions, cloud-based digital solutions, application programming interfaces, and model context protocol servers. The company serves professionals, including institutional asset managers, bankers, wealth managers, asset owners, partners, hedge funds, corporate users, private equity and venture capital professionals. FactSet Research Systems Inc. was founded in 1978 and is headquartered in Norwalk, Connecticut.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Sanoke  Viswanathan | CEO & Director | Age 50 | Compensation: $17.4M (FY2026)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 12K people. Revenue per employee of $199K ranks in the bottom quartile among Financial Services peers, with revenue growing 9%/yr across its filed history. Each employee generates $57K of free cash flow annually. Stock-based compensation of $7K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 87\u00d7 revenue per employee (high relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags elevated compensation governance risk (8/10).","financial_summary":["FactSet Research Systems Inc. is a large-cap financial services business with a $11.7B market cap on $2.5B of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +6% over the past three years and +8% annually across the full decade, a respectable pace for a business of this size.","Returns on capital run at 21% against a 8% cost of capital \u2014 a 12-point spread that is the clearest signature of an economic moat.","The business throws off $707M in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 29 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders, and cash conversion sits at 1.54\u00d7 so those profits are backed by real cash.","On the balance sheet, leverage is comfortably conservative at 1.3\u00d7 net debt/EBITDA, and interest coverage of 13\u00d7 is fortress-like.","Management returns a meaningful 6.9% of market cap to owners through dividends and buybacks, a strong signal of disciplined capital allocation, and insider ownership is negligible, so management has little personal stake in the long-term outcome."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Low reinvestment-driven growth suggests the compounding engine has stalled","sev":"amber","cat":"growth"},{"text":"Trading near 52-week highs \u2014 the market has already recognised the story (confirmed by 2 other valuation measures)","sev":"amber","cat":"valuation","magnitude":0.37382413087934574},{"text":"Volatile returns on capital suggest the moat is narrower than a snapshot ROIC implies","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Elevated short interest (12.6% of float) \u2014 sophisticated money is betting the other way","sev":"amber","cat":"sentiment"},{"text":"Credit cycles and regulatory capital \u2014 losses accumulate invisibly in good years and appear all at once, and the time to worry is when underwriting standards are loosest.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Fintech disintermediation \u2014 neobanks, embedded finance, and blockchain rails are unbundling the fee streams that traditional banks took for granted.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Interest rate regime shifts \u2014 a rapid move in rates can invert the yield curve, crush bond portfolios, and trigger deposit flight simultaneously.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Altman Z comfortably in the safe zone \u2014 a fortress balance sheet on this measure","27 consecutive years of dividend payments \u2014 an operating record that makes the dividend claim credible","Healthy payout ratio leaves room for both dividend growth and reinvestment"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"FactSet Research Systems (FDS) Could Be 28% Overvalued On Its AI And Data Push","source":"simplywall.st","link":"https://simplywall.st/stocks/us/diversified-financials/nyse-fds/factset-research-systems/news/factset-research-systems-fds-could-be-28-overvalued-on-its-a","date":"2026-11-13","timestamp":1794579475.947,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.883,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Cellebrite DI Investigation Notice: Levi & Korsinsky Notifies Investors of Pending Investigation Into Cellebrite DI (CLBT)","source":"prnewswire.com","link":"https://www.prnewswire.com/news-releases/cellebrite-di-investigation-notice-levi--korsinsky-notifies-investors-of-pending-investigation-into-cellebrite-di-clbt-302939345.html","date":"2026-11-13","timestamp":1794612960.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.0,"tier":2,"scope":"company","tags":["legal"]},{"title":"Wall Street forecasters see tumbling corporate earnings hobbling the stock market in 2027","s